Refactor this code by combining the map/filter pair into one comprehension:

def labels(values):
    kept = filter(lambda v: v is not None, values)
    return list(map(lambda v: v.strip(), kept))

output:
def labels(values):
    return [v.strip() for v in values if v is not None]

What changed: two higher-order passes (and two lambdas) collapsed into one comprehension with the filter on the right and the mapping on the left.

